===Etymology 2===
{{ja-kanjitab|yomi=juku|あす2}}

From {{inh|ja|ojp|sort=あす|-}}, first attested in the ''{{w|Kojiki}}'' (712 {{CE}}).

Various theories exist regarding the ultimate derivation:
* Possibly a shift from verb {{m|ja|明かす|tr=akasu||to [[pass]]}}.
*: {{IPAfont|*/akasu/}} → *{{IPAchar|/akusu/}} → {{IPAchar|/asu/}}
* Possibly an [[apophony|apophonic]] form of or cognate with {{m|ja|朝|tr=asa||[[morning]]}}.

The kanji spelling is an {{obor|ja|zh|nocap=1|明日}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{ja-pron|あす|acc=2|acc_note=''as a noun''|acc_ref=NHK,DJR,SMK5,<ref name="NKD2O_asu"/>|acc2=0|acc2_note=''as an adverb''|acc2_ref=NHK,<ref name="NKD2O_asu"/>}}
{{ja-accent-dialectal|region=Kyoto|k|あ|す|áꜜsù|ref=<ref name="KHK"/><ref name="NKD2O_asu">{{R:ja:NKD2O|あす 【明日】|lid=200200148947P4Ij8o9R|kotobank=明日-424515#w-1865844}}</ref>}}{{attention|ja|平進 Heishin? It's a rise then a fall, instead of koki which is mostly/all rises IMO}}
{{ja-accent-historical|h=LL|e=HL|ref=<ref name="NKD2O_asu"/>}}

====Noun====
{{ja-noun|あす}}

# {{lb|ja|polite}} [[tomorrow]]
#* {{RQ:ja:AB|000035/files/275_13903}}
#*: {{ja-usex|'''明日'''も[[また]]、[[同じ]][[日]]が[[来る]]のだろう。[[幸%福]]は[[一%生]]、[[来る|来]]ないのだ。[[それ]]は、[[わかる|わかって]]いる。[[けれども]]、[[きっと]][[来る]]、'''あす'''は[[来る]]、と[[信じる|信じて]][[寝る]]のが[[いい]]のでしょう。|'''あす''' も また、おなじ ひ が くる の だろう。こう%ふく は いっ%しょう、こない の だ。それ は、わかっている。けれど も、きっと くる、'''あす''' は くる、と しんじて ねる の が い.い の でしょう。|The same day will probably come '''tomorrow''' again, just like always. True happiness will never come into my life. I know that. But perhaps it is best to go to sleep believing that it will come, that it will come '''tomorrow'''.}}
